From 456b09cd3224054fcc9bb189992662ca7848fe00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huicong Zhang <wytrocheung207@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:57:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Adapt Nanoset dataloader to public datatrove 0.5.0
 signature

nanotron 0.4's "new dataloader" (upstream 1dfee7f, SmolLM3) was written against a
HuggingFace-INTERNAL datatrove fork whose DatatroveFolderDataset accepted extra
kwargs (max_tokens, eos_token_id, read_path, matched_files, file_sizes). No public
datatrove release or main provides that signature (verified against 0.3.0/0.4.0/
0.5.0/0.9.0 and main). Adapt nanotron to the PUBLIC signature instead.

Pinned env: datatrove[io]==0.5.0, numpy==2.0.2, huggingface_hub<1.0, pybind11
(0.5.0 is the newest datatrove exposing positions_from_eos_token_id that still
allows hub <1.0, required by transformers 4.46.3 / tokenizers 0.20.3).

Four sites:
1. nanoset.py: eos_token_id= -> positions_from_eos_token_id= (1:1 semantics).
2. tokenized_bytes.py super().__init__: same rename; drop max_tokens/read_path/
   matched_files/file_sizes (HF-fork-only S3 offload, per-dataset cap, cached
   file list -- irrelevant for local-disk data).
   LIMITATION: per-dataset dataset_max_tokens is no longer enforced; keep it None.
3. tokenized_bytes.py: restore self.folder_path as a str -- public datatrove sets
   it to a DataFolder object but nanotron's consumption/offset accounting compares
   it as a string.
4. blendable_dataset.py get_consumption_stats: drop assert "s3" in folder_path
   (already marked "TODO: remove this" upstream) so local-disk folders work.

Plus the multi-epoch fix:
5. tokenized_bytes.py __getitem__: wrap with item % len(self). Public datatrove's
   DatatroveFolderDataset.__getitem__ indexes files directly with NO wrap, so
   item >= len(self) walks bisect off the file list -> IndexError at EXACTLY the
   1-epoch boundary (S0 10B data: step ~4768, consumed_tokens 10.0B). nanotron's
   own TokenizedBytesFileDataset / OldTokenizedBytesFolderDataset already wrap;
   this subclass lost it when re-pointed at the public class. Required for the
   3-epoch / 30B runs.

See PATCH_NOTES.md for the full write-up.
